==Finnish==

===Pronunciation===
*Hyphenation: ka·to
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:Finnish:-ɑto|-ɑto]]
*{{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈkɑto]}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably the source of {{term|kadota||to disappear|lang=fi}}, cognate with Estonian {{term|kadu||loss|lang=et}}.

{{etystub}}

====Noun====
{{fi-noun|ka|type=mato}}

# [[failure|Failure]] of [[crop]]s.
# [[loss|Loss]], [[disappearance]].

===Etymology 2===
A dialectal or colloquial imperative of {{term|katsoa||to look|lang=fi}}, whose infinitive would be {{term|kattoa}}.

====Verb====
'''kato'''

# {{colloquial|lang=fi}} [[look]]!
#:'''''Kato''', tuolla on [[neekeri]]!'' &mdash; ''Look, there's a [[negro]]!''
# {{colloquial|lang=fi}} [[see]]
#:'''''Kato''', ei [[neekeri]] ole haukkumasana.'' &mdash; ''See, [[negro]] is not a pejorative word.''

====Interjection====
{{fi-int}}

# {{colloquial|lang=fi}} [[see]] or [[look]].
#*''Se on '''kato''' sillä lailla.''
#**'''''See''', that’s the way it is.''
#*'''''Kato''' nääs!'' or '''''Kato kato!'''''
#**Literally: ''Look, look!.'' Uttered in surprise, not necessarily telling anyone to look anywhere.
#*''...'''kato''' nääs.'' or ''...'''kato.''''' 
#**''...you see.'' (At the end of a sentence)

